Now that the repository architecture is in place, develop **Phase 0 in vertical slices**, not folder-by-folder. The order below keeps every implementation aligned with the final Enterprise Financial & Profit Intelligence Infrastructure.

### 1. Application foundation

Develop first:

```text
CfoApplication.java

platform/config/
├── ApplicationProperties.java
├── JacksonConfig.java
├── TransactionConfig.java
├── AsyncConfig.java
└── OpenApiConfig.java


platform/web/
├── GlobalExceptionHandler.java
├── ApiErrorResponse.java
├── ApiResponse.java
├── CorrelationIdFilter.java
└── RequestLoggingFilter.java


shared/domain/
├── Money.java
├── CurrencyCode.java
├── DateRange.java
├── TenantId.java
├── UserId.java
├── OrganizationId.java
├── SourceReference.java
└── VersionedValue.java


shared/exception/
└── all exception classes
```


**Goal:** application starts cleanly, has consistent API errors, IDs, money representation, request correlation and basic enterprise conventions.

